From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: soc: sunxi: cpu_comm: no read of the MIPS status behind a closed bus gate

Without an owner bound (sun50i-h713-mips missing, its probe failed, or
unbound after a park) cpu_comm_mips_running() read the MIPS status word
raw, and prepare and suspend_late asked it at every sleep - after a raw
park, whose last write closes the block's bus gate (0x0200160c bit 0),
such a read hangs the bus. Two guards: prepare and suspend_late look at
the software state first (parked, or stopped for a restart: no core to
refuse for or to park, no register touched), and the raw read itself
happens only while the CCU shows the clock on and the gate open - the two
words the raw park writes, always readable. With the owner bound, as on
every image, nothing changes. Review of 09.10.2026, CC-6.

Not measured at the device (needs a sleep without the owner).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c
@@ -1516,6 +1516,30 @@
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(cpu_comm_set_mips_owner);
 
+#define H713_CCU_MIPS_CLK	0x02001600	/* 0x80000002 running, 0 off */
+#define H713_CCU_MIPS_RESET	0x0200160c	/* 0x00070001 released, 0 held */
+#define H713_MIPS_PARK_MS	12
+
+/*
+ * Without an owner, the MIPS block is reachable only while the CCU shows
+ * its clock on and its bus gate open (the two words the raw park writes
+ * to 0 below); behind a closed gate a read of the status word hangs the
+ * bus. The CCU itself is always there to read (review 09.10., CC-6).
+ */
+static bool cpu_comm_mips_block_reachable(void)
+{
+	void __iomem *ccu;
+	bool reachable;
+
+	ccu = ioremap(H713_CCU_MIPS_CLK, 0x10);
+	if (!ccu)
+		return false;
+	reachable = (readl(ccu) & BIT(31)) &&
+		    (readl(ccu + (H713_CCU_MIPS_RESET - H713_CCU_MIPS_CLK)) & BIT(0));
+	iounmap(ccu);
+	return reachable;
+}
+
 bool cpu_comm_mips_running(void)
 {
 	bool up;
@@ -1524,7 +1548,7 @@
 	if (cpu_comm_mips_owner)
 		up = cpu_comm_mips_owner->alive(cpu_comm_mips_owner->ctx);
 	else
-		up = mips_ctrl_base &&
+		up = mips_ctrl_base && cpu_comm_mips_block_reachable() &&
 		     (readl(mips_ctrl_base + MIPS_REG_STATUS) & BIT(0));
 	mutex_unlock(&cpu_comm_mips_owner_lock);
 	return up;
@@ -1536,9 +1560,6 @@
  * when one is bound; otherwise the registers are written raw here, as the
  * R1 park did, because nobody else holds them then.
  */
-#define H713_CCU_MIPS_CLK	0x02001600	/* 0x80000002 running, 0 off */
-#define H713_CCU_MIPS_RESET	0x0200160c	/* 0x00070001 released, 0 held */
-#define H713_MIPS_PARK_MS	12
 
 int cpu_comm_mips_park(u32 *clk, u32 *rst)
 {
